-- Castle Nathria (map 2296) -- ground-hazard persistent-area-auras (15).
-- The generic SL->3.3.5 spell downport (14) clamped these 12 'CREATE_AT' spells' effects to
-- 0 (modern spawned-AreaTrigger creator effects have no equivalent in this fork's 3.3.5 Effect
-- enum, so they were safety-clamped away by the same LoadSpellInfoStore-limit guard as any
-- other unmappable effect). The 10 boss C++ files already CAST these spells at fixed ground
-- positions (see each boss_*.cpp's TODO(port) comments) expecting a real ground hazard --
-- this file authors that hazard directly as a SPELL_EFFECT_PERSISTENT_AREA_AURA (27) +
-- SPELL_AURA_PERIODIC_TRIGGER_SPELL (23) combo (same technique retail itself uses for many
-- ground-pool mechanics before spawned-AreaTriggers existed): a DynamicObject is created at
-- the cast destination (ImplicitTargetA=TARGET_DEST_DEST=87) and periodically re-casts the
-- paired damage/debuff spell (already a real, non-clamped downport from file 14) on anyone
-- standing in its radius. Radius/duration indices are existing LIVE 3.3.5 SpellRadius.dbc /
-- SpellDuration.dbc rows (14=8yd, 29=6yd; 8=15s, 18=20s, 85=18s) -- no new index rows needed.
--
-- This OVERRIDES 12 rows already inserted by 14_boss_spells_dbc.sql / 15_boss_spells_dbc_addendum.sql
-- for the same ids -- must run AFTER both (apply_all.sql already orders it that way). Mirrors the same override into the
-- client Custom/CSV DBC/Spell.csv (recompiled+deployed alongside this file).
--
-- Apply to acore_world.

DELETE FROM `spell_dbc` WHERE `ID` IN (340299,329002,342865,334889,332375,329620,325718,327125,335371,348698,328658,326275);

